      "writtenOn": "2023-04-11T17:53:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In SkImage.h, there are readPixels functions without this that are deprecated.\n\nIf we had two versions (of this function), clients could pass a GPU-backed image to the the one without the context parameter and be puzzled why we fail silently (because we cannot read the pixels out of their image for encoding). \n\nThus, I think it\u0027s best that users intentionally set nullptr if they are dealing with raster images. A good API is hard to be used wrong.",
